      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on current cleaning and changeover practices and main issues.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 558848,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, let's kick off the Cross-Line Hygiene project. To start, can we map out our current processes? For the food lines, let's detail the cleaning and changeover steps as part of T1. @310108, could you do the same for the metal sawing area for T2?",
            "mentions": [
              310108,
              102838,
              433963,
              462838,
              527555
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "rocket",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 433963,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Good start. For the food lines, the process is roughly: 1. Air-jet blowout of dry debris. 2. Lockout/Tagout. 3. Pre-rinse with hot water. 4. Foam application with detergent. 5. Manual scrub of contact surfaces. 6. Final rinse. 7. Sanitize. 8. Air dry. The biggest pain point is the manual scrubbing on Line 2, it always takes longer than expected.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "heavy_plus_sign",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 310108,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "For the metal saw area (T2), it's simpler. We power down, use compressed air to blow chips off the machine body and into the collection tray, sweep the floor, and wipe down the guards. The main issue is fine metal dust settling on walkways that are shared.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 462838,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Also sometimes we have to wait for maintenance if a guard is stuck, that adds time.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 102838,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "what about the bottle washer?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 433963,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "That has its own CIP cycle, it's mostly automated. We can add that as a separate sub-task under T1.",
            "mentions": [
              102838
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 558848,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Thanks both. This is great info. We'll need to pilot the new procedures. I suggest we use Food Line 3 since it's our most standard setup, and for the metal area, maybe the main band saw? @310108 what do you think?",
            "mentions": [
              310108
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 310108,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "The main band saw works. It gets the most use, so it's a good test case.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "ok_hand",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 527555,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Line 3 is fine.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 558848,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Perfect. Let's lock that in. Decision: We will use Food Line 3 and the main band saw for the pilots.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 433963,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "To measure improvement, we need to use the Time Tracking Sheet A4. What key phases should we capture for both areas?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 102838,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "just start and end time?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 558848,
            "reply_to": "M12",
            "text": "We need more detail to find bottlenecks. I propose we track: 'Preparation', 'Gross Cleaning', 'Detailed Scrub/Wash', 'Rinsing/Wipe-down', and 'Sanitizing/Final Checks'. This structure should work for both food and metal areas.",
            "mentions": [
              102838
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
            "speaker_id": 310108,
            "reply_to": "M13",
            "text": "That works for the saw. 'Gross Cleaning' would be blowing off the big chips, and 'Detailed Scrub/Wash' would be wiping the guards and surfaces.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M15",
            "speaker_id": 433963,
            "reply_to": "M13",
            "text": "Agreed. That covers all our key stages. We should also add a column for 'Notes' to capture any unexpected delays.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M16",
            "speaker_id": 558848,
            "reply_to": "M15",
            "text": "Excellent point. Okay, decision confirmed: The time tracking sheet A4 will capture 'Preparation', 'Gross Cleaning', 'Detailed Scrub/Wash', 'Rinsing/Wipe-down', 'Sanitizing/Final Checks', and a 'Notes' column.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "clap",
