      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Define rules for shared equipment and forklift hygiene between areas.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 558848,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Let's discuss shared equipment, especially forklifts. I've seen them move directly from the metal area to food packaging, and we need a clear rule to prevent cross-contamination. This is for task T4.",
            "mentions": [
              310108,
              433963,
              102838,
              462838,
              527555
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "warning",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 310108,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Good point. The forklift tires can pick up a lot of metal shavings. We can't have those near the food lines. We need a designated cleaning spot or procedure before it enters the food zone.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 433963,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Absolutely. We need a simple, quick checklist for this, as described in A3. It has to be fast, or people will skip it during busy periods. I'm thinking a visual inspection, a tire brush-down, and a wipe of the forks.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "brain",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 102838,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "do we have to wash the whole thing?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 558848,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "A full wash isn't practical for every trip. @433963's suggestion sounds like a good minimum standard. What does everyone else think about 'inspect, brush tires, wipe forks' as the rule before entering food areas?",
            "mentions": [
              433963,
              102838
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 310108,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "That's feasible. We can set up a small station with an air hose and some rags near the crossover point. It shouldn't take more than 2-3 minutes.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 462838,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "sounds good",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 558848,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Okay, let's make that official. Decision: The minimum cleaning steps before a forklift enters food areas are: visual inspection, brushing/blowing off tires, and wiping down forks.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 433963,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Now, how do we make sure it's done? Should we log it every time? That seems like a lot of paperwork.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 527555,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "that is a lot",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 558848,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "I agree. How about this: we add it to the operator's daily pre-shift forklift inspection checklist. They just have to check a box confirming they know the rule and have the supplies ready. We can then do spot checks during the shift rather than logging every single crossing.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 310108,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "That's more practical. A daily sign-off makes sense. It becomes part of the routine.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 433963,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "I like that. It reinforces the habit without creating a bottleneck. So we're logging it once per shift, per operator, as part of their standard equipment check.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 558848,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "Exactly. Decision confirmed: Shared equipment hygiene checks must be logged once per shift as part of the operator's pre-use inspection.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "clap",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 433963,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "Great. I will update the draft for A3, the Shared Equipment Checklist, with these rules. I should have it ready for review this afternoon.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3",
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          }
        ],
